FEATURE: skeleton-module
DATE: 2026-10-05
SCOPE: add vUX-skeleton.js, placeholder screens derived from the consumer's own
       template, and fix Component.sync() without onMount, found along the way

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) is the only project affected. Apps that symlink it
(vGet, app.myinvitees.com) get the module on their next page load, and nothing
changes for them unless they import it.

Consumer-visible surface:
  - vUX-skeleton.js           new module: Skeleton
  - assets/css/skeleton.css   its stylesheet, linked at import
  - src/helpers.js            module registry entry
  - vUX-component.js          bug fix: sync() without config.onMount
  - doc/skeleton.md           new guide
  - examples/skeleton/        new example page

Additive, apart from the Component fix. No member was renamed or removed and no
existing call signature changed. The fix changes behaviour only where it was
wrong: sync() without onMount used to return undefined per row and destroyAll()
left those rows in the page.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WAS BUILT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

new Skeleton(container); config.template (a <template> or element, or null for
mask mode), count, animation (shimmer | pulse | none), delay, minDuration,
colors, radius, label, reveal, onShow, onHide; initialize(), show(), hide() ->
Promise, during(promise) -> Promise, destroy(), and a read-only state.

Template mode derives ghosts from the template (fields -> bars, media -> blocks,
controls -> blocks, structure kept) into a layer beside the container. Mask mode
masks existing content in place and reverses every change. data-skeleton
overrides the inference per element.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No test runner exists in vUX. Verified in headless Chrome (Windows Chrome driven
from WSL; the Linux headless shell lacks system libraries):
  - a scratch harness of 27 checks, all passing;
  - the example page scripted through every section with no uncaught errors;
  - screenshots reviewed at 1280px; no horizontal overflow at 390px.
Not tested: Firefox, Safari (including the iOS fallback for fixed backgrounds).
